{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאמר אלעזר הכהן", :translit "vayomer el'azar ha-kohen", :gloss "And said Elazar the priest"} {:he "משה דבר לראשי האלפים", :translit "moshe diber l'rashei ha-alafim", :gloss "Moses spoke to the heads of the thousands"} {:he "פרשת טהרה", :translit "parshat taharah", :gloss "the section of purity"} {:he "דיני גיעול", :translit "dinei gi'ul", :gloss "laws of purging"} {:he "ההזאה", :translit "ha-haza'ah", :gloss "the sprinkling"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between Moses' audience (commanders) and Elazar's audience (soldiers) explains why Elazar, not Moses, taught the laws of purging."}], :frame {:text "Numbers 31:21-24 records that Elazar the priest instructed the returning soldiers regarding purging (גיעול) metal vessels taken as spoil. Numbers 31:6 states that the holy vessels and signaling trumpets were in the hands of Elazar when the army went to battle. The Talmud derives that the laws of kashering captured vessels were spoken specifically through Elazar, while Moses addressed the commanders. The passage of purification in Numbers 31:19-20 was addressed by Moses to the troops, but the specific halakha of purging vessels (v. 21) is introduced as Elazar's teaching.", :sources ["Numbers 31:6" "Numbers 31:19-20" "Numbers 31:21-24" "Chullin 115a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between Moses' audience (commanders) and Elazar's audience (soldiers) explains why Elazar, not Moses, taught the laws of purging.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:18.821105243Z", :model "glm-5.2"}